// T5 — The design follows the conversation, and nothing is destroyed
// Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md ("S:n" = its line n) and the accepted ADRs docs/adrs/SIFT-ADR-0*.md.
// Founder ruling 2026-11-04: Source = "Spec of record". NDD-SOURCE.md is a derived document: it gives the thread structure and the titles only; where it differs from the spec, the spec wins.
//
// STORY FLOW (founder ruling bd996f3e, 2026-11-07, "15 story flows, branches inside"): the main path runs from the start of the thread to its T5.O5 terminal, in the order the spec tells it.
// Every alternative of the thread, once a flow of its own, is a branch at the moment where it diverges: a [branch] moment that holds its deciding event as a plain node (moved from the main path, not copied), an empty first arm `TheMainPath` (the walk takes the first arm when none is chosen, so the main path is the one that goes on after the moment) and one `when` arm for each alternative,
// each ending at its own exit ([outcome] when it is a normal outcome of the thread, [terminal] for a failure or a refusal) or falling through into the moments that follow. Moment derives one scenario for each path. A refusal is a precondition of a command; Moment 0.9.0 derives its negative scenario for every path of the flow (ADR-042). A branch moment that nothing precedes (the first node of the flow, or one whose deciding event is the only node of the previous branch moment's main arm) keeps its first arm `TheMainPath` with the main path's next nodes: no event to anchor on (docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md, 0.9.0 rework).
// A branch arm cites the former flow it carries in its first comment line (the old-to-new mapping is in docs/sidd/round30/story-flows-log.md).
// BRANCHES:
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementAnswerKeepsTheConstruct (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-answer-keeps-the-construct.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementAnswerNamesAnXThatIsNotLive (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-answer-names-an-x-that-is-not-live.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementAnswerOnABoundaryConstructByAnOperatorIsRatifiedInline (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-answer-on-a-boundary-construct-by-an-operator.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementAnswerOnABoundaryConstructProposesTheChange (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-answer-on-a-boundary-construct-proposes.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementAnswerReplacesTheConstructByX (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-answer-replaces-the-construct-by-x.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementQuestionIsAnswered (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-answered.moment)
//   T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: AVersionRetirementQuestionIsWithdrawnWhenTheNewVersionRestatesItsConstructs (former flow t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-withdrawn-when-the-version-restates-its-constructs.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: ADroppedWordRetiresATerm (former flow t5-a-dropped-word-retires-a-term.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AStatedReplacementIsAskedAsARetirement (former flow t5-a-stated-replacement-is-asked-as-a-retirement.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AStatedReplacementListsTheMembersOfTheRetiredArm (former flow t5-a-stated-replacement-lists-the-members-of-the-retired-arm.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AStatedReplacementUnderSourceAuthorityConversationRetiresNothing (former flow t5-a-stated-replacement-under-source-authority-conversation.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AStatedReplacementUnderSourceAuthoritySiftRetiresX (former flow t5-a-stated-replacement-under-source-authority-sift.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: ASteerOnAStatedReplacementIsAnsweredContinue (former flow t5-a-steer-on-a-stated-replacement-is-answered-continue.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: ASteerOnAStatedReplacementIsAnsweredReturn (former flow t5-a-steer-on-a-stated-replacement-is-answered-return.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AnAnswerReplacesTheConstructByAnother (former flow t5-an-answer-replaces-the-construct-by-another.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AnAnswerRetiresTheConstruct (former flow t5-an-answer-retires-the-construct.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: TheAnswersSuccessorWasNotOfferedOrXIsNoLongerLive (former flow t5-the-answers-successor-was-not-offered.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: TheEntryStatesWhatItNegatesAndXIsABoundaryType (former flow t5-the-entry-states-what-it-negates-and-x-is-a-boundary-type.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: TheEntryStatesWhatItNegates (former flow t5-the-entry-states-what-it-negates.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: TheEntryStatesWhatItReplacesAndXIsABoundaryType (former flow t5-the-entry-states-what-it-replaces-and-x-is-a-boundary-type.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: TheEntryStatesWhatItReplaces (former flow t5-the-entry-states-what-it-replaces.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AMemberOfARetiredArmIsMovedToCByTheAnswer (former flow t5-a-member-of-a-retired-arm-is-moved-to-c.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted: AnAggregateMemberOfARetiredBCIsMovedToCByAProposal (former flow t5-an-aggregate-member-of-a-bc-is-moved-to-c-by-a-proposal.moment)
//   T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted (continued): TheSuccessorIsTheConstructItselfIsNotLiveOrIsNotTheHeadOfIts (former flow t5-the-successor-is-the-construct-itself-or-is-not-live-or-not-head.moment)
//   T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn: TheArmIsReDerivedForABCWithNoAggregate (former flow t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-for-a-bc-with-no-aggregate.moment)
//   T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn: TheArmIsReDerivedInADifferentContext (former flow t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-in-a-different-context.moment)
//   T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn: TheArmIsReDerivedInTheSameContext (former flow t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-in-the-same-context.moment)
// REFUSALS REACHED BY A PRECONDITION on a command of the flows above (a derived `neg-<Command>-<Precondition>` scenario): StoreConstruct.NoOpRepeat; SupersedeConstruct.SupersessionRefused and
// .NoOpRepeat (T5.M5·B1 "X is not live"); RefuseSupersession.Self, .NotLive and .NotHead (T5.M2·B1's three reasons); MootGap.AnyNonTerminal; ApplyAnswer.DeferredOrStale.
// DIFFERENCES FROM NDD-SOURCE (the spec wins): the NDD draws "P3.54 StartPass(Live) evaluates TAC-013 ... a Gap asks which supersession was meant" with the refusal; the spec has the Live pass find a
// TAC-013 Gap of kind Plain (S:681, S:722), so the refusal flow runs the pass to GapOpened and the question (audit D-9); NDD T5.M3 lists the arm re-derivation (P3.38) as part of one chain, the spec gives
// it as four cases (S:595-599), each its own branch; the `PTR` crossing and "SUPERSEDED_BY edge" of NDD T5.M6 are flmnt's side (the spec says the Sift pointer supersedes the pointer, S:659).
// carried from the former main flow, its header: The remaining branches of the answers and cases are other threads: Keep -> none (holds for the asking document version only, S:527); a boundary construct -> Propose(retire | replace) (T13); one X that
// Part of the model directory; validate with `moment parse model/` (project mode) and `moment test` on this file.

flow "T5 — The design follows the conversation, and nothing is destroyed"
  description "T5 — The design follows the conversation, and nothing is destroyed. The story of the thread from its start to its T5.O5 outcome, with its alternatives as branches at the moment where each diverges. Source of record: docs/sidd/round30/pass7-domain-spec.md."

  lane design "DesignModel" [Core]
  lane clarification "Clarification" [Core]
  lane intake "Intake" [Core]

  moment "T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // [person] a person records a decision that supersedes or replaces an earlier one (T2 path, then T3.M1..M3)  // S:493 "**Supersedes** (non-boundary) → StoreConstruct(supersedes X)"
      // A user's decision.superseded of a Sift pointer: lineage reads the pointer as the construct it names, the divergence gate passes it, and the user's construct supersedes Sift's without being asked back  // S:663 "so the user's construct supersedes Sift's without being asked back"
      // A flmnt split (one entry superseded by 2-8 components) arrives as N entries, each placed on its own  // S:505 "Each is placed on its own: the first decided Supersedes supersedes the construct"
      design: PlacementDecided  // S:436 "PlacementDecided {outcome, rationale, alternatives[]};"
    when AVersionRetirementAnswerKeepsTheConstruct
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-answer-keeps-the-construct.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its header: Alternative drawn in the close-out (S4 sweep, "Separate flows"): a row of the version-retirement answer (S:1112) that t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-answered (Retire) did not draw. Rows are exclusive alternatives, so each is its own flow.
      // carried from the former flow, its header: DocumentVersionProcessed (the close) is a process event of DocumentIntake (S:397); the AskQuestion is the reaction of policy RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion (S:521).
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved [outcome]  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      // Keep → none: no command, no event follows the resolved question  // S:1112 "Keep → none (the recorded answer holds for the asking document version only"
      // A later document version's close lists the construct again  // S:1112 "a later document version's close lists the construct again"
    when AVersionRetirementAnswerNamesAnXThatIsNotLive
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-answer-names-an-x-that-is-not-live.moment
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      // T5.M5 · The construct is asked again
      // an X that is not live leaves the construct unchanged: no SupersedeConstruct  // S:1112 "an X that is not live leaves the construct unchanged and not kept"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:1112 "so it is asked again as the next generation (Answers, above), and the answerer gets a notice"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "Retirement by omission (Round 27 A-1" (policy RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked [outcome]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
    when AVersionRetirementAnswerOnABoundaryConstructByAnOperatorIsRatifiedInline
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-answer-on-a-boundary-construct-by-an-operator.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T5 — the answerer is an operator: the Propose carries ratifiedBy and is proposed and ratified in one write; the ratification supersedes the construct and starts a model-wide Convergence pass. Spec of record S:1112, S:850, S:885, S:733."
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: Propose  // S:1112 "ContextMap Propose(retire, or replace by X, source: that Pointer, created constructs: none, ratifiedBy if the answerer is an operator)"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1111 "a PlacementDecided gathered by a retirement question" (policy RoutingRetirementAnswerProposes)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:850 "BoundaryChangeProposed{ratifiedInline}"
      design: BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:850 "BoundaryChangeRatified in one write"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeRatified  // S:885 "SupersedeConstruct(by: successor | none, cause: Ratified) for each construct the change retires" (policy BoundaryChangeRatifiedSupersedesRetired)
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}"
      design: StartPass  // S:733 "a BoundaryChangeRatified of a Propose(rename), a Propose(retire) or a replace that creates none) → StartPass(Convergence, scope: the customer workspace, model-wide)"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:397 "run the policies of DocumentVersionProcessed in their listed order (§11.1): StartPass(Document, scope: the constructs the document version's sections placed) first" (policy DocumentVersionProcessedStartsDocumentPass)
      design: PassStarted [outcome]  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
    when AVersionRetirementAnswerOnABoundaryConstructProposesTheChange
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-answer-on-a-boundary-construct-proposes.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, its description: description "T5 — the answer retires or replaces a boundary construct: the change is a ContextMap Propose with no created constructs, and an operator is asked to ratify it. Spec of record S:1112, S:880."
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: Propose  // S:1112 "on a boundary construct, either → ContextMap Propose(retire, or replace by X, source: that Pointer, created constructs: none"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1111 "a PlacementDecided gathered by a retirement question" (policy RoutingRetirementAnswerProposes)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      // T5.M5 · An operator is asked
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:881 "otherwise all architects (cascading to admins and owners when there are none)"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked [outcome]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
    when AVersionRetirementAnswerReplacesTheConstructByX
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-answer-replaces-the-construct-by-x.moment
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:1112 "replaced by X → SupersedeConstruct(by: X, cause: Answered, Pointer: that Pointer), where X is a live construct"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question" (policy RoutingVersionRetirementAnswerSupersedes)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:555 "ConstructSuperseded {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, when there is a successor"
      design: ConstructLinked [outcome]  // S:558 "given a Pointer records it with ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated"
    when AVersionRetirementQuestionIsAnswered
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-answered.moment
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes and asks what it no longer states
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      design: RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:521 "AskQuestion (subject: the **version-retirement subject** for V, §4: V's Pointer qualified as retirement"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionAsksQuestion
      clarification: QuestionAsked  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule"
      // [person] a recipient answers the version-retirement question (received and recorded as T4.M3..M4)  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question (Round 27 A-1)"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Answer  // S:1028 "ResolveQuestion(answer + request Pointer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy)"
      clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:1112 "Retire → SupersedeConstruct(by: none, cause: Answered, Pointer: the Pointer of the asking document version)"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1112 "a DocumentVersionProcessed gathered by a version-retirement question" (policy RoutingVersionRetirementAnswerSupersedes)
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}"
      design: ConstructLinked [outcome]  // S:558 "given a Pointer records it with ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated"
    when AVersionRetirementQuestionIsWithdrawnWhenTheNewVersionRestatesItsConstructs
      // former flow: t5-a-version-retirement-question-is-withdrawn-when-the-version-restates-its-constructs.moment
      // T5.M5 · A document version closes
      intake: DocumentVersionProcessed  // S:521 "DocumentVersionProcessed for a document version V of documentId D (the close, §2 Document intake step 4)"
      // T5.M5 · The question of an earlier version is withdrawn
      design: RetirementByOmissionWithdrawsQuestion  // S:527 "(2) ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for each generation of an open version-retirement question of an earlier document version of D"
        triggered-by DocumentVersionProcessed
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Withdrawn  // S:527 "(2) ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for each generation of an open version-retirement question of an earlier document version of D that is left with no listed construct"
        triggered-by RetirementByOmissionWithdrawsQuestion
      clarification: QuestionResolved [outcome]  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy"

  moment "T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      // Supersedes -> StoreConstruct(supersedes X), unless X is terminal when the store runs (then without supersession)  // S:493 "unless X is terminal when the store runs (then without supersession)"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:546 "StoreConstruct(Pointer, proposedFor?, supersedes?);"
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:493 "Supersedes (non-boundary) → StoreConstruct(supersedes X)" (policy SupersedesOutcomeStoresConstruct)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      // ConstructLinked{Placed} is recorded with the store; the Stored(supersedes) policy then issues SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this, cause: Successor), which records ConstructLinked{Supersedes} on X  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this, cause: Successor"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always, with the Placement's Pointer)"
    when ADroppedWordRetiresATerm
      // former flow: t5-a-dropped-word-retires-a-term.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: [person] a document version's glossary section or owner sentence drops a word  // S:520 "a glossary section or an owner sentence of the newest document version of its document whose candidate drops a word"
      // T5.M4 · The entry says what it replaces or negates
      // for each live Term of that word, ApplyAnswer(computed{dropped-word}) on that Term's Placement, recorded as AnswerApplied{outcome: Retire, computedBy: dropped-word}; the computed answer re-opens the decided Placement (the ApplyAnswer invariant)  // S:520 "for each live Term of that word, ApplyAnswer(computed{dropped-word}) on that Term's Placement"
      design: ApplyAnswer  // S:520 "ApplyAnswer(computed{dropped-word}) on that Term's Placement"
        triggered-by PlacementDecided  // S:520 "Dropped word (Round 28; c9256057):" (policy DroppedWordAppliesComputedAnswer)
      design: AnswerApplied  // S:437 "AnswerApplied {outcome, question | computedBy: rule, trigger}"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:494 "for the dropped-word computed answer, SupersedeConstruct(by: none, cause: Stated, Pointer: the trigger entry's Pointer) on the Term whose Placement the answer is applied to"
        triggered-by AnswerApplied  // S:494 "Retire (an architect's answer to a Defer question" (policy RetireOutcomeSupersedesProvisional)
      design: ConstructInvalidated [outcome]  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, for by: none"
    when AStatedReplacementIsAskedAsARetirement
      // former flow: t5-a-stated-replacement-is-asked-as-a-retirement.moment
      // S: citations of the former flow that its nodes do not repeat (kept, none dropped):
      // carried from the former flow, T5.M1 · A later decision changes an earlier one: [person] a person records a deciding entry whose candidate states what it replaces or negates  // S:513 "**Stated replacement (ruling b187882c, Round 21):** each case below is its own policy with its own predicate and one command"
      // T5.M4 · The entry says what it replaces or negates
      // exactly one X and this entry is not a deciding entry, or several -> listed in the retirement question for this entry (subject: this entry's Pointer qualified as retirement; recipients: all architects, cascading to admins and owners)  // S:516 "exactly one, and this entry is not a deciding entry, or several → listed in the **retirement question for this entry**"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:516 "(AskQuestion, subject: this entry's Pointer qualified as retirement, §4; causedBy: this event"
