      design: BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:851 "else → BoundaryChangeProposed"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:881 "otherwise all architects (cascading to admins and owners when there are none)"
        triggered-by BoundaryChangeProposed  // S:880 "BoundaryChangeProposed (not ratifiedInline, not withdrawn in the same write)" (policy BoundaryChangeProposedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked [outcome]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?}"

  moment "T5.M2 · The old construct is superseded, not deleted (continued)" [branch]
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:549 "SupersedeConstruct(by?, cause: Successor | Ratified | Rejected | SubjectChanged | Answered | Stated"
        triggered-by ConstructStored  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this" (policy StoredSupersedesSupersedesPredecessor)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:555 "ConstructSuperseded {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, when there is a successor"
    when TheSuccessorIsTheConstructItselfIsNotLiveOrIsNotTheHeadOfIts
      // former flow: t5-the-successor-is-the-construct-itself-or-is-not-live-or-not-head.moment
      // Outcome: SupersedeConstruct(by) names the construct itself, or a construct that is terminal or not the head of its lineage, so the supersession is refused and recorded (SupersessionRefused); nothing is superseded and the Live pass finds it as a TAC-013 Gap that asks which supersession was meant.
      // T5.M2·B1 · when the successor is the construct itself, is terminal, or is not the head of its lineage
      // when the successor is the construct itself, is terminal, or is not the head of its lineage: the policy that would issue SupersedeConstruct issues RefuseSupersession(construct, by, reason Self | NotLive | NotHead) instead; nothing is superseded  // S:648 "the policies that issue SupersedeConstruct (the Stored(supersedes) policy, the stated-replacement and stated-negation policies, retirement routing), when the successor fails the guard → RefuseSupersession instead of SupersedeConstruct;"
      design: RefuseSupersession  // S:614 "RefuseSupersession(construct, by, reason: Self | NotLive | NotHead), system-only."
      design: SupersessionRefused  // S:620 "SupersessionRefused {by, reason}."
      // SupersessionRefused -> the Live pass that evaluates TAC-013 on the construct whose supersession was refused  // S:722 "**SupersessionRefused** (§3 Lineage; Round 28, 73d00215 (pass-1 B-2); this is the one definition of the policy, and §3 Lineage cites it) → StartPass(Live, scope: the construct whose supersession was refused"
      design: StartPass  // S:722 "→ StartPass(Live, scope: the construct whose supersession was refused"
        triggered-by SupersessionRefused  // S:722 "SupersessionRefused (§3 Lineage; Round 28" (policy SupersessionRefusedStartsLivePass)
      design: PassStarted  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
      design: RecordGateResults  // S:669 "RecordGateResults(sequence number, evaluated constructs[], findings[])"
        triggered-by PassStarted  // S:720 "Gate run: PassStarted → GateRun" (policy PassStartedRunsGates)
      // TAC-013 is a catalogue rule (family Tactical, handling Ask, cadence Live): the finding is of kind Plain  // S:681 "the finding is of kind Plain"
      design: GapIdentified  // S:673 "GapIdentified {GapKey {rule, construct, origin}"
      design: ObserveGap  // S:744 "ObserveGap(pass, startPosition, finding, origins, CauseKey), system-only, and only from a pass"
        triggered-by GapIdentified  // S:721 "GapIdentified → ObserveGap" (policy GapIdentifiedObservesGap)
      design: GapOpened  // S:750 "GapOpened {handling, pass, finding, carriedFrom?};"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:809 "**Ask** → AskQuestion (subject: GapKey; causedBy: this event; recipients: all architects, cascading to admins and owners"
        triggered-by GapOpened  // S:809 "Ask → AskQuestion (subject: GapKey" (policy GapHandlingAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked [terminal]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?};"

  moment "T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn" [branch]
    design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "given a Pointer records it with ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated"
    when TheMainPath
      // the main path of the story: no node here, the deciding event is the plain node above; the main path goes on in the moment that follows (founder ruling "Yes, anchor the branches": the deciding event is moved into the branch moment, the arm carries none of the main path's nodes)
    when TheArmIsReDerivedForABCWithNoAggregate
      // former flow: t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-for-a-bc-with-no-aggregate.moment
      // T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn
      // a ConstructInvalidated of an Aggregate construct (terminal with no successor), for each live Invariant or Event whose arm it was -> the arm is re-derived: resolve the Invariant's current enforcedBy (or the Event's current producer) to its arm  // S:595 "**The arm re-derived** (Round 27 A-11, ruling \"Re-derive the arm\")"
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, for by: none"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:598 "a BC with no Aggregate resolved → the successor is stored with that context and no arm, which is a provisional and a missing-arm question"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:595 "The arm re-derived (Round 27 A-11" (policy ArmReDerivedSameContextOnInvalidatedAggregate)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      clarification: AskQuestion  // S:501 "**for a Defer recorded for a missing context or arm, the missing-arm subject**"
        triggered-by ConstructStored  // S:528 "Missing arm arrived (ruling f9025299" (policy MissingArmArrivedAsksQuestion)
      clarification: QuestionAsked [outcome]  // S:1033 "QuestionAsked {generation, causedBy, recipientRule, CorpusVersion, SubjectVersions shown?};"
    when TheArmIsReDerivedInADifferentContext
      // former flow: t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-in-a-different-context.moment
      // T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn
      // a ConstructInvalidated of an Aggregate construct (terminal with no successor), for each live Invariant or Event whose arm it was -> the arm is re-derived: resolve the Invariant's current enforcedBy (or the Event's current producer) to its arm  // S:595 "**The arm re-derived** (Round 27 A-11, ruling \"Re-derive the arm\")"
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, for by: none"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:597 "the resolved Aggregate, or the resolved BC, is in a **different bounded context** → StoreConstruct(the Invariant′, proposedFor: BoundaryRatification)"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:595 "The arm re-derived (Round 27 A-11" (policy ArmReDerivedSameContextOnInvalidatedAggregate)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      design: Propose  // S:597 "ContextMap Propose(move X: A → B, source: that Pointer, created constructs: the Invariant′), ratified as any proposal"
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed [outcome]  // S:1332 "BoundaryChangeProposed | AskQuestion (ratification)"
    when TheArmIsReDerivedInTheSameContext
      // former flow: t5-the-arm-is-re-derived-in-the-same-context.moment
      // T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn
      // a ConstructInvalidated of an Aggregate construct (terminal with no successor), for each live Invariant or Event whose arm it was -> the arm is re-derived: resolve the Invariant's current enforcedBy (or the Event's current producer) to its arm  // S:595 "**The arm re-derived** (Round 27 A-11, ruling \"Re-derive the arm\")"
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, for by: none"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:596 "the resolved Aggregate is in the Invariant's current context → StoreConstruct(the Invariant's content with that arm, supersedes the Invariant"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:595 "The arm re-derived (Round 27 A-11" (policy ArmReDerivedSameContextOnInvalidatedAggregate)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this, cause: Successor"
        triggered-by ConstructStored  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this" (policy StoredSupersedesSupersedesPredecessor)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:596 "**The move is recorded by the successor's ConstructStored and the Invariant's ConstructSuperseded (cause Successor) with ConstructLinked{Supersedes}: no new event**"
      design: ConstructLinked [outcome]  // S:558 "given a Pointer records it with ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated"
    when TheArmIsReDerivedInTheSameContextAfterAMarkedSameAs
      // T5.M3 · a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant's enforcedBy or an Event's producer re-derives the arm
      // a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant's enforcedBy or an Event's producer, its first owner -> the arm is re-derived: resolve the Invariant's current enforcedBy (or the Event's current producer) to its arm  // S:595 "a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant"
      design: MarkSameAs  // S:1104 "a SameAs answer on non-boundary constructs → MarkSameAs (with the addition the answer names, if any; Round 13), then DisposeGap(Resolved{SameAs})"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1104 "a SameAs answer on non-boundary constructs → MarkSameAs" (policy RoutingSameAsAnswerMarksSameAs)
      design: MarkedSameAs  // S:557 "MarkedSameAs {LineageLink, addition?}"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:596 "the resolved Aggregate is in the Invariant's current context → StoreConstruct(the Invariant's content with that arm, supersedes the Invariant"
        triggered-by MarkedSameAs  // S:595 "a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant" (policy ArmReDerivedSameContextOnMarkedSameAs)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      design: SupersedeConstruct  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this, cause: Successor"
        triggered-by ConstructStored  // S:590 "Stored(supersedes X) → SupersedeConstruct(X, by: this" (policy StoredSupersedesSupersedesPredecessor)
      design: ConstructSuperseded  // S:596 "**The move is recorded by the successor's ConstructStored and the Invariant's ConstructSuperseded (cause Successor) with ConstructLinked{Supersedes}: no new event**"
      design: ConstructLinked [outcome]  // S:558 "given a Pointer records it with ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated"
    when TheArmIsReDerivedInADifferentContextAfterAMarkedSameAs
      // T5.M3 · the same re-derivation, the resolved arm in a different bounded context: never a silent move
      // a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant's enforcedBy or an Event's producer, its first owner -> the arm is re-derived: the resolved Aggregate, or BC, is in a different bounded context  // S:595 "a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant"
      design: MarkSameAs  // S:1104 "a SameAs answer on non-boundary constructs → MarkSameAs (with the addition the answer names, if any; Round 13), then DisposeGap(Resolved{SameAs})"
        triggered-by QuestionResolved  // S:1104 "a SameAs answer on non-boundary constructs → MarkSameAs" (policy RoutingSameAsAnswerMarksSameAs)
      design: MarkedSameAs  // S:557 "MarkedSameAs {LineageLink, addition?}"
      design: StoreConstruct  // S:597 "the resolved Aggregate, or the resolved BC, is in a **different bounded context** → StoreConstruct(the Invariant′, proposedFor: BoundaryRatification)"
        triggered-by MarkedSameAs  // S:595 "a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant" (policy ArmReDerivedSameContextOnMarkedSameAs)
      design: ConstructStored  // S:552 "ConstructStored {Arrival, attempt};"
      design: ConstructLinked  // S:558 "StoreConstruct records it with ConstructStored (Placed; always"
      design: Propose  // S:597 "ContextMap Propose(move X: A → B, source: that Pointer, created constructs: the Invariant′), ratified as any proposal"
        triggered-by MarkedSameAs  // S:595 "a MarkedSameAs whose addition replaces an Invariant" (policy ArmReDerivedOtherContextProposesMove)
      design: BoundaryChangeProposed [outcome]  // S:1332 "BoundaryChangeProposed | AskQuestion (ratification)"
    when AnInvalidatedConstructMootsItsGapsAndWithdrawsItsQuestions
      // T5.M3 · a ConstructInvalidated moots every non-terminal Gap on the construct and withdraws the questions whose constructs are all terminal
      design: ConstructInvalidated  // S:556 "ConstructInvalidated {cause, Pointer?, pass?}, for by: none"
      design: MootGap cause ConstructEvent  // S:747 "MootGap(cause: construct event | Evaluated | Erased), system-only"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:593 "MootGap for every Gap on that construct that isn" (policy ConstructInvalidatedMootsGaps)
      design: GapMooted  // S:755 "GapMooted {cause} (Round 27 A-7: the cause MootGap carried"
      clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Withdrawn  // S:594 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for every open question generation that gathers or lists constructs"
        triggered-by ConstructInvalidated  // S:594 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for every open question generation that gathers or lists constructs" (policy ConstructInvalidatedWithdrawsAllTerminalQuestions)
      clarification: QuestionResolved [outcome]  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy, request Pointer?};"

  moment "T5.M3 · What depended on it is re-assessed and what asked about it is withdrawn (main path)"
    // the main path of the story
    // ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated, as three policies on the one event, each issuing one command  // S:591 "ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated, as three policies on the one event, each issuing one command"
    design: StartPass  // S:592 "StartPass(Invalidation, dependents);"
      triggered-by ConstructSuperseded  // S:591 "ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated, as three policies on the one event" (policy ConstructSupersededStartsInvalidationPass)
    design: PassStarted  // S:672 "PassStarted {startPosition, CorpusVersion, RulesVersion}"
    design: MootGap cause ConstructEvent  // S:593 "MootGap for every Gap on that construct that isn't terminal"
      triggered-by ConstructSuperseded  // S:593 "MootGap for every Gap on that construct that isn" (policy ConstructSupersededMootsGaps)
    design: GapMooted  // S:755 "GapMooted {cause}"
    clarification: ResolveQuestion cause Withdrawn  // S:594 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for every open question generation that gathers or lists constructs and whose gathered or listed constructs are now all terminal"
      triggered-by ConstructSuperseded  // S:594 "ResolveQuestion(Withdrawn) for every open question generation that gathers or lists constructs" (policy ConstructSupersededWithdrawsAllTerminalQuestions)
    clarification: QuestionResolved  // S:1034 "QuestionResolved {generation, resolution: an answer | Withdrawn{WithdrawalCause}, answeredBy, request Pointer?};"
    // A link field or an arm that names the superseded construct is read as the successor through the lineage; nothing is rewritten  // S:580 "the read-through is the rule"

  moment "T5.M6 · The conversation sees the change"
    // [flmnt] the Sift pointer: a construct that has a Sift pointer, superseded or invalidated by any cause, writes a Sift pointer that supersedes the current head of each named entry's chain (`recordSiftPointer`, not declarable)  // S:659 "a ConstructSuperseded or ConstructInvalidated of a construct that has a Sift pointer, whatever its cause, narrative included (P2-G2) → kind supersedes"
    // The agent workspace takes the construct's entry superseded; each construct entry supersedes that construct's previous entry  // S:1423 "each construct entry stamped with its construct ID and superseding that construct's previous entry (Round 24)"
    design: AgentWorkspace [terminal]  // S:1423 "each construct entry stamped with its construct ID and superseding that construct's previous entry (Round 24)"

  moment "T5.O5 · The design followed the conversation (terminal)"
    // PROVES: ConstructSuperseded {cause, Pointer} with ConstructLinked{Supersedes} recorded; moots and withdrawals done; the Sift pointer superseded; no Kurrent event removed or rewritten (never destructive); the history is still readable in the graph  // S:583 "Never destructive."
    note design: "The graph read model folds ConstructStored, ConstructAccepted, ConstructCommitted, ConstructSuperseded, ConstructInvalidated, MarkedSameAs and ConstructLinked"  // S:1417 "graph | ConstructStored · ConstructAccepted · ConstructCommitted · ConstructSuperseded · ConstructInvalidated"
